<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.2.1: Finding the Percent of 200</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00070</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.2.1: Finding the Percent of 200</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d2548bdf-9a30-4ee8-91aa-f96cfa793d82</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>You will be asked to evaluate the percentage of a number mentally. Sometimes, a visual is helpful to do this. If needed, use the GeoGebra activity to help you determine the requested values. Then, look for a pattern that can be used to describe how to find the percentage of any number. </para>
<media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://www.geogebra.org/material/iframe/id/XSFd8GkK/width/1035/height/468/border/888888/sfsb/true/smb/false/stb/false/stbh/false/ai/false/asb/false/sri/false/rc/false/ld/false/sdz/false/ctl/false"/></media><section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="89acbc05-bc17-40cb-9872-c5ce8a7fb71f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para> What is 25% of 200? </para>
      </problem><solution><para> Correct! 50</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 50</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="7b37d976-9dba-4f13-af94-03b694dd688f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para> What is 12% of 200? </para>
      </problem><solution><para> Correct! 24</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 24</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="dd65ceb4-46ec-46c7-830f-cdeeec095223" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para> What is 8% of 200? </para>
      </problem><solution><para> Correct! 16</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 16</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- Q4 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>How would you determine \( p \)% of \( 200 \)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <list>
      <item>\(2p\)</item>
      <item>\(\frac{p}{100} \cdot 200\)</item>
      <item>Change the percentage to a decimal and multiply it by 200.</item>
      <item>Since percent means “per hundred” and there are two hundreds, the percentage is multiplied by two.</item>
    </list>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!-- Interaction End -->
</section>
